<body>
  <h1>Zucchini Banana Oatmeal Choc Chip Muffins</h1>
  <p><em>Yield: 24 muffins</em></p>
  
  <h2>Ingredients</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>4 cups shredded zucchini</li>
    <li>3 cups all-purpose flour</li>
    <li>1.5 cups old-fashioned rolled oats</li>
    <li>5 tsp ground cinnamon</li>
    <li>3 tsp baking powder</li>
    <li>1 tsp baking soda</li>
    <li>1 tsp kosher salt</li>
    <li>4 very ripe bananas, mashed</li>
    <li>1 cup pure maple syrup</li>
    <li>4 large eggs</li>
    <li>1.5 cups vegetable oil</li>
    <li>4 tsp vanilla extract</li>
    <li>1.5 cups chocolate chips</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Instructions</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Preheat oven to 350°F (175°C). Line two muffin tins with paper liners.</li>
    <li>Wrap the shredded zucchini in a clean kitchen towel and squeeze out as much excess water as possible. Set aside.</li>
    <li>In a very large bowl, whisk together flour, oats, cinnamon, baking powder, baking soda, and salt.</li>
    <li>In a separate large bowl, stir together mashed bananas, maple syrup, eggs, oil, and vanilla until fully combined.</li>
    <li>Pour the wet ingredients into the dry ingredients and stir until just combined—don't overmix.</li>
    <li>Gently fold in the drained zucchini and chocolate chips until evenly distributed.</li>
    <li>Scoop about 1/3 cup of batter into each liner. Bake for 24 to 28 minutes, until a toothpick inserted into the center comes out with a few moist crumbs but no wet batter.</li>
    <li>Let muffins cool in the pan for 10 minutes, then transfer to a wire rack to cool completely.</li>
  </ol>
